module std;

import core;

// Forge hosted standard-library root.
//
// `std` is layered on `core`. Hosted startup, console I/O, filesystem,
// networking, clocks, OS threads, entropy, and allocator/provider
// implementations live behind platform/provider contracts rather than leaking
// target APIs into portable application code.
//
// Hosted execution does NOT create an implicit/default allocator policy for
// ordinary APIs. Any operation that allocates, grows, clones owning storage, or
// frees durable storage receives an explicit allocator argument at that call.
// Ordinary strings/collections/buffers never retain allocator capabilities.
//
// Bootstrap hosted modules currently include:
//   std.console
//   std.args
//   std.fs
//   std.lock
//   std.time
//   std.string
//
// The root does not implicitly re-export these modules. Applications import
// only the hosted services they use. File/lock/time/argument operations end in
// target platform providers; portable collection/string algorithms belong in
// Forge source as the compiler/runtime substrate becomes capable enough.
